Homepage redesign (September 2026)
---------------------------------
The homepage now focuses on team activity, footage and the crew. It uses
home.css, leaving the existing account/store styles in styles.css intact.
No build step is required. Netlify can publish the repository root.

Latest video cards use the existing YouTube configuration; if the API fails,
the featured video and permanent channel/social links remain available.
Calendar, poll and discussion are retained as expandable sections.
Netlify contact form processing must be verified on a Netlify preview; it
cannot be exercised with a file preview or GitHub Pages.

Before publishing:
- Confirm the current team roster/roles and the featured YouTube video.
- Add actual car names, photos and build details to cars.html; its original
  placeholder entries are still present. Driver photos also need replacement.
- Confirm Netlify's production branch and enable a deploy preview for review.
- Rotate/revoke the former Snipcart secret key; removing it from config.js
  does not remove it from Git history or previously deployed copies.
- Verify Firebase sign-in, store checkout, calendar, poll and discussion with
  their real service accounts. Homepage no longer initializes Firebase or
  touches login controls before they exist; member login remains accessible.

Members and admins (September 2026)
----------------------------------
See MEMBER_ADMIN_SETUP.md for Firebase setup, owner assignment and data paths.
The new portal uses portal.js / portal.css; existing profile/editor addresses
remain supported. Admins can manage homepage media, updates, member roles,
member media and store products. Videos are HTTPS links or YouTube embeds.

Verified locally:
- Firebase Firestore/Storage emulator permission suite in tests/permissions.cjs.
- Profile/avatar retention and content/link safety in tests/frontend.cjs.
- JavaScript syntax, page links, unique IDs and whitespace checks.

To reproduce from the repository root:
  npm install --prefix tests --no-audit --no-fund
  NODE_PATH=tests/node_modules node tests/frontend.cjs
  NODE_PATH=tests/node_modules tests/node_modules/.bin/firebase emulators:exec --project demo-imob-rules --only firestore,storage 'node tests/permissions.cjs'

Backend setup and real-account/browser verification remain required before
production. Publishing the Netlify preview does not publish Firebase rules.
